  "conclusion": "The explicit capability and frontmost-first correction passed every pre-target gate except canonical protected-readiness-observer reproduction. A post-preflight no-GUI audit reproduced SHA-256 9662c1664d44e93f58dc690a0fb78f08eb1f4751d84fc5790256866e768811ce with the authoritative issue #98 build. The differently ordered/output-named f2c9b54561c68d8dea89ced7253316b7e1604db1b2eac42683e7d1609be4f023 artifact supplied to the preflight was noncanonical and never executed. The sole preflight retained exact identity and successfully wrote supported/settable AXFrontmost=true once, but Accessibility readback remained supported false and Workspace remained not frontmost through the unchanged 20-second bound. Minimized and frame reads remained explicitly unavailable/attribute-unsupported. No AXMinimized write, AXRaise, independent observer, product setup, retry, or issue #104 consumption occurred."
